  "term": "immaterialism",
  "definition": "Immaterialism is the view, associated especially with Berkeley, that only conscious beings or spirits have true independent existence. On this account, the material world does not exist as a separate substance but only as perceived experience or an ordered set of signs through which minds relate to one another.",
